  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-lab art direction, disciplined cyan/yellow accents, crisp borders, and a clear headline-to-results hierarchy. Desktop feels polished, but the oversized headline and broad empty right side make the opening composition unbalanced. Tablet is cohesive; mobile becomes overly tall and dense, with tiny metadata, awkward headline wrapping, and a crowded evidence card. The actual tablet/mobile headers visibly clip the navigation; mobile also loses the wordmark and red-mode action. Contrast proof is incomplete across many header elements, so full polish is not established.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero, reduce mobile headline and card density, raise small-text contrast and size, and replace clipped header navigation with an intentional responsive menu or scroll treatment that preserves the wordmark and primary action.",
